  "scope": "Focused independent mathematical and exact-source review of GCF7--GCF11 only. Existing PA1--PA2 and TA1,TA5,TA11 are inherited human proofs. No family-realization or broader global-compatibility closure is inferred from this focused review.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "torsion_action",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The simultaneous eta scaling and m^2=eta^-1 normalize both invariants exactly; CM transport acts on algebraic curve identities and differentials, not on analytic limits under arbitrary complex automorphisms."
    },
    {
      "id": "g3_sign",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The two complementary idempotents on two-torsion and the supplied unkilled point give a unique labelled class. The discriminant-square polynomial is fixed and nonzero, forcing eta^3=1. The ideal-lattice existence argument works for all original nonzero ideals."
    },
    {
      "id": "g2_cubic",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "Trace zero modulo3 supplies a class outside the two eigenspace kernels. The actual beta involution on the four nonzero three-torsion abscissae, the quartic identity, and the vanishing cubic coefficient force the squared-pair-sum invariance. Thus v^3=1 and G/v descends."
    },
    {
      "id": "given_field_and_delta",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "FieldOK supplies G^3,T^2 and the CM scalars. Fixed-field descent and the original Base inclusion of Q(mu_(3^4)) put both invariants in the same coefficient image for the originally prescribed delta; no field or period replacement remains in the actual endpoint."
    },
    {
      "id": "omega_normalization",
      "result": "PASS",
      "detail": "The original ellT is the same mapped different-ideal span. The chosen generator and all infinity labels are retained. Conjugate lattices differ by a twelfth root of unity, preserving area, and the positive guard is inactive. The pi*norm^2/area inverse is precisely all literal OmegaCompatible fields and omTied_withTrue for every later W,V,S,N."
    }
  ],
